// ADR 0071 M1.4a slice 3 / filed-defect register D31: the REFCOUNT CLONE on a container
// argument to a GENERIC function.
//
// A `Shared<T>` / `Mutex<T>` handle passed BY VALUE to a user fn transfers a refcount
// unit, so the caller must emit `rc++` (`sentinel_shared_clone`) to balance the `rc--`
// the callee emits at scope exit. `scg` did that in `dump_targs` — the ordinary-call arg
// walker — and NOT in `dump_args_capture_all`, the GENERIC-call walker, whose own comment
// claimed it mirrored `dump_targs`. So a container passed to a generic fn got no clone
// while the callee still released it: one release too many, the cell freed while the
// caller still held it, and the caller's next read a use-after-free. The oracle always
// emitted the clone, which is why a NON-generic callee was byte-identical and this hid.
//
// The load-bearing invariant is `#new + #clone == #release` — measured on the minimal
// repro as oracle 1/1/2 (balanced) against `scg` 1/0/2 (one short). Each binding below
// exercises a different corner of the one broken walker:
//   - `takes_one(s)`         the base shape: a container as the only argument.
//   - `takes_second(9, s)`   NOT in first position — the walker recurses, so a fix that
//                            only handled the head argument would pass the base shape.
//   - `takes_two(s, t)`      two containers in one call: two independent clones.
//   - `takes_one(m)`         the `Mutex` branch of the helper, a separate arm from
//                            `Shared` emitting `sentinel_mutex_clone`.
//
// TWO NEGATIVE cases matter more than any of those, because each pins one half of the
// decision; before ADR 0071 D2 amendment A1 a wrong implementation that dropped either passed
// every positive case above AND the rest of the corpus, and `c71_shared_place_duplications`
// now pins both as well:
//   - `takes_zero(shared_new(1))`  an RVALUE source. It TRANSFERS its unit, so the oracle
//                                  emits NO clone. Since ADR 0071 D2 amendment A1 the
//                                  decision is `dump_texpr_node`'s: only a node that reads
//                                  out of a place is cloned. Let a call's node claim to be
//                                  one and this over-clones — a permanent leak, D31's
//                                  mirror image.
//   - `Holder::With(u)`            an ENUM-CONSTRUCT payload (below).
//
// A COMPOUND argument whose tail is a binding (`takes_one({ s })`) was a third negative
// case before A1: the oracle cloned only a bare binding, and `scg`'s `ndump` leaf test
// existed to match that. It could not be written here then, for a reason outside `scg`. A1
// made it a duplication like any other (a block hands the owning context to its tail), so
// the oracle and `scg` both clone it now, and the `ndump` test is gone from that path.
//
// The enum payload: `Holder::With(u)` is an enum-CONSTRUCT argument, not a user-fn owning
// param. Its walker, `dump_cargs`, is asked not to own there, so `cg_ufarg` stays off and
// the payload gets no owning context; turn it on and it over-clones. The codegen differential
// pins that here and on `c71_shared_place_duplications`'s `E::A(s)`.
//
// ⚠ THE EXIT CODE CANNOT CATCH THIS DEFECT AT ALL, and saying "it is the weaker
// assertion" would understate it. `run_exit` builds through inkwell, which emitted the
// clone correctly the whole time; `scg`'s IR is never linked into anything this harness
// runs. So the exit code exercises the back end that was always right. **The codegen
// differential is the ONLY thing that pins this** — it sweeps `tests/pass` and compares
// `scg` against the oracle byte-for-byte. If this file is ever "simplified" by trusting
// the exit code, the fixture stops testing anything.
//
// For the record on severity, since the runtime makes it sharper than "a divergence":
// `sentinel_shared_release` does `fetch_sub` then `debug_assert!(prev >= 1)`, and frees
// at `prev == 1`. At the PREMATURE release `prev` IS 1 — so the assert passes, the cell
// is freed while an owner is still live, and nothing reports it. The assert can only fire
// on a LATER release, which is by then a write to freed memory with a garbage `prev`.
//
// ⚠ DELIBERATELY ABSENT, because they hit DIFFERENT defects and would pin those instead:
// a generic that RETURNS its container param (`fn ident<T>(x: T) -> T`), and a generic
// that passes its param to another generic. Both still emit different IR in the oracle and
// `scg` (register D36: the oracle hands a moved generic parameter on, `scg` clones it and
// releases the parameter — balanced either way since ADR 0071 D2 amendment A1), so the
// codegen differential would fail on them. Do not "complete" this fixture with either.
//
// Trace: 7 + 9 + 9 + 7 + 0 (the rvalue negative case) + 6 (s) + 4 (t) = 42.
// Exit 42, no stdout.

fn takes_one<T>(x: T) -> i64 {
    7
}

fn takes_second<T>(a: i64, x: T) -> i64 {
    a
}

fn takes_two<T>(x: T, y: T) -> i64 {
    9
}

// Contributes 0 so the negative cases below leave the trace arithmetic alone.
fn takes_zero<T>(x: T) -> i64 {
    0
}

enum Holder {
    Empty,
    With(Shared<i64>),
}

fn main() -> i64 {
    let s: Shared<i64> = shared_new(6);
    let t: Shared<i64> = shared_new(4);
    let m: Mutex<i64> = mutex_new(3);

    let a: i64 = takes_one(s);
    let b: i64 = takes_second(9, s);
    let c: i64 = takes_two(s, t);
    let d: i64 = takes_one(m);

    // The two NEGATIVE cases. Each must emit NO clone; see the header.
    let e: i64 = takes_zero(shared_new(1));
    let u: Shared<i64> = shared_new(0);
    let h: Holder = Holder::With(u);

    // Both handles are still live here — that is the whole point. Pre-fix the refcount
    // had already reached zero and these two reads were reading freed memory.
    a + b + c + d + e + shared_get(s) + shared_get(t)
}
